'''Grabvine Gateway''' was a [[podracing]] course<ref name="Beyond Victory">[[Star Wars: Beyond Victory - A Mixed Reality Playset|''Star Wars: Beyond Victory'' - A Mixed Reality Playset]]</ref> in [[Baroonda (city)|Baroonda]].<ref name="Ever Been to Ghorman?" /> The [[Snivvian]] [[Podracer (profession)|podracer]] [[Coy Vrizh]] had won a race on the course by the [[time]] he competed on the [[Hydian-Hutta Podracing Circuit]]<ref name="Beyond Victory" /> around [[10 BBY]].<ref name="Date">{{BeyondVictoryDate}}</ref> The win was recorded on Vrizh's downloadable racing profile.<ref name="Beyond Victory" /> When [[Syril Karn]] attempted to gain entry to the [[Imperial office complex]] on the [[planet]] [[Ghorman]] after [[Standard hour|hours]] in [[3 BBY]], the building's [[Unidentified Imperial office complex guard 1|two]] [[Unidentified Imperial office complex guard 2|guards]] were watching a podrace on a [[datapad]] screen, with [[Aurebesh]] text at the bottom indicating that the race took place at Grabvine Gateway.<ref name="Ever Been to Ghorman?" />

==Behind the scenes==
Grabvine Gateway first appears in the ''[[Star Wars: Andor]]'' episode "[[Ever Been to Ghorman?]]"<ref name="Ever Been to Ghorman?" /> In the [[Star Wars Legends|''Star Wars'' Legends]] continuity, the location originated in the [[1999]] [[LucasArts]] [[Star Wars video games|video game]] [[Star Wars: Episode I Racer|''Star Wars'': Episode I ''Racer'']].<ref name="EpIRacer">[[Star Wars: Episode I Racer|''Star Wars'': Episode I ''Racer'']]</ref>

